lines for businesses\",\"company Wikipedia guidelines\",\"Wikipedia notability for companies\",\"Wikipedia neutral point of view\",\"Wikipedia reliable sources\"],\"hasPart\":{\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can a business write its own Wikipedia article?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"A business can gather sources and understand the process, but direct involvement can raise conflict-of-interest concerns. Neutrality, reliable sourcing, and transparent handling of paid or connected editing are important considerations.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What content should a business article include?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"It should include only information supported by reliable independent sources, presented neutrally and proportionately. The exact content depends on what sources cover, not what the business wants to promote.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Do Wikipedia guidelines guarantee approval if followed?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"No. Following guidelines improves quality and compliance, but independent Wikipedia editors make final decisions about content, inclusion, and retention.\"}}]}}c:[[[\"$\",\"script\",\"0\",{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"WebPage\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/wikipedia-article-guidelines-for-businesses#webpage\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Wikipedia Article Guidelines for Businesses\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Key Wikipedia guidelines businesses should understand before creating or editing an article, including notability, neutrality, sourcing, and disclosure.\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/wikipedia-article-guidelines-for-businesses\\\",\\\"isPartOf\\\":{\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https://miqllcwiki.com/#website\\\"},\\\"about\\\":{\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https://miqllcwiki.com/#organizatio